# CMake
cmake-build-debug/
cmake-build-release/
build/
bin/
lib/
# BUILD TREES AND INSTALL PREFIXES BY POLICY, NOT BY ENUMERATION.
#
# These used to be listed one directory at a time, and the comment here said
# so outright: build-host/ and install-host/ each with "own name, own ignore
# line" as the stated shape. THAT ENUMERATION FELL BEHIND THREE TIMES --
# build-pb/, build-ci-consumer/ and install-ci/ were each untracked and NOT
# ignored. The last two are the expensive ones: they made every provenance
# line on 2026-09-10 report dirty=true, across every realm, in a phase whose
# recurring subject was whether a tally's provenance could be trusted at all.
#
# The root .gitignore reached this conclusion for ROOT trees and states the
# reason above its own /build-*/ rule: "An enumeration was guaranteed to fall
# behind the moment the parameter existed, and did, within the hour." That
# comment has been sitting one directory away from an enumeration doing
# exactly that.
#
# A pattern needs no guard, which is the point: an enumeration can only be
# kept current by someone remembering, so it needs a test to catch them
# forgetting. This cannot fall behind.
#
# SAFE because nothing under spade/ that is not a build artifact begins with
# build- or install-: the real directories are assets/ cmake/ docs/ engine/
# examples/ include/ scripts/ src/ tests/ vendor/. A future source directory
# wanting one of those prefixes has to say so here, which is the right place
# for that argument to happen.
#
# What these cover, since the names no longer explain themselves:
#   build-host/ + install-host/  scripts/spade-prefix.ps1's scratch build and
#                                the cmake --install prefix dronesim/spade's
#                                find_package(spade) resolves against
#   build-ci/ + install-ci/      the docker gate's own spade leg + its
#                                out-of-tree consumer smoke
#   build-ninja/<preset>/        spade/scripts/build.ps1's dev-loop trees
#
# NOTE: the ROOT .gitignore also lists spade/build-ci/ and spade/build-ninja/
# individually. Those entries are now redundant rather than wrong, and they
# are not mine to remove.
build-*/
install-*/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
*.cmake
# Exception (S5 T9 ticket B): a genuine, committed CMake HELPER SCRIPT, not a
# build-tree-generated artifact -- *.cmake above exists for the latter
# (CMake's own generated Find*.cmake/config files live under build-ninja/,
# already excluded by build/ above; this blanket pattern is broader than it
# needs to be, but narrowing it further is out of this ticket's scope).
!tests/AppendSpadeLabels.cmake
# Same exception, same reason (S6 Task 3): cmake/SpadeSlang.cmake is an
# authored, committed helper -- the D9 shader build's two functions -- that the
# blanket *.cmake pattern above would otherwise hide from `git status`
# entirely, so it could only ever be committed with `git add -f` and would
# silently stop being tracked for edits. Nothing GENERATED is un-ignored here:
# the D9 generated headers (layout_check.gen.hpp, bindings.gen.hpp,
# <kernel>.spv.gen.hpp) and the .spv artifacts live under build-ninja/, already
# excluded by build/ above, and are deliberately never committed.
!cmake/SpadeSlang.cmake
Makefile

